## Why This Is Asked

This question tests practical, scalable cache invalidation across services, covering Redis pub/sub, versioned keys, and cross-tenant isolation.

## Key Concepts

- Cache-aside vs write-through
- Versioned keys: item:{id}:v and item:{id}
- Redis pub/sub for coordinated invalidation
- Stampede prevention: refresh locks and TTL tuning

## Code Example

```javascript
// Write path (pseudo)
function updateItem(id, value){
  const vKey = `item:${id}:v`;
  const valueKey = `item:${id}`;
  const newV = Date.now();
  redis.incr(vKey);
  redis.set(valueKey, value, 'EX', 60);
  redis.publish('invalidation', JSON.stringify({id, v:newV}));
}
```

```javascript
// Read path (pseudo)
async function readItem(id){
  const vKey = `item:${id}:v`;
  const valueKey = `item:${id}`;
  const currentV = await redis.get(vKey) || 0;
  let value = await cache.get(valueKey);
  if(!value){
     value = db.query(id);
     cache.set(valueKey, value, 60);
  }
  const cachedV = parseInt(await redis.get(vKey) || '0', 10);
  if(currentV > cachedV){
     value = db.query(id);
     cache.set(valueKey, value, 60);
     redis.set(vKey, currentV);
  }
  return value;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you tune TTLs for latency vs staleness across tenants?
- How would you rotate keys and migrate tenants without downtime?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests hands-on ability to bridge IdP types, enforce strict audience/issuer boundaries, and implement robust replay and revocation protections in a real-world gateway.

## Key Concepts

- SAML assertion validation and attribute mapping
- OIDC token exchange and PKCE considerations
- JWT issuance with tenant-scoped aud/iss and JWKS rotation
- Redis-backed revocation with TTLs
- Token binding: device nonce + TLS cert fingerprint to prevent replay

## Code Example

```javascript
// Issuer: extract claims, map to internal JWT
function issueInternalJwt(claims, nonce, thumbprint) {
  const payload = { sub: claims.user_id, tenant: claims.tenant, aud: claims.tenant + '.service', iss: 'internal.auth', nonce, thumbprint, scopes: claims.scopes }
  return jwt.sign(payload, keystore.getKey(), { algorithm: 'RS256', expiresIn: '15m' })
}
function verifyInternalJwt(token, expectedThumbprint) {
  const decoded = jwt.verify(token, keystore.getPublicKey(), { algorithms: ['RS256'] })
  if (decoded.thumbprint !== expectedThumbprint) throw new Error('fingerprint mismatch')
  return decoded
}
```

