## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates the candidate's ability to handle cross-service compensation, drift recovery, and per-tenant isolation in a Saga-driven, event-sourced architecture.

## Key Concepts
- **Saga Orchestration**: Coordinating distributed transactions with compensating actions
- **CQRS & Event Sourcing**: Managing read/write separation and handling state drift
- **Outbox Pattern**: Ensuring reliable event publication for replay after failures
- **Idempotency**: Preventing duplicate processing with tenant-scoped keys
- **Per-Tenant Thresholds**: Custom anomaly handling per tenant

## Code Example
```javascript
// Orchestrator skeleton
class RefundOrchestrator {
  constructor(outboxStore, tenantConfig) {
    this.outbox = outboxStore;
    this.config = tenantConfig;
  }

  async start(orderId, tenantId) {
    const tenant = this.config.get(tenantId);
    await this.outbox.append({
      type: 'RefundCommand',
      orderId,
      tenantId,
      maxRetries: tenant.maxRefundRetries,
      timeoutMs: tenant.refundTimeoutMs
    });
  }

  async onRefundResult(evt) {
    if (evt.status === 'success') {
      await this.completeOrder(evt.orderId, evt.tenantId);
    } else {
      await this.triggerCompensation(evt.orderId, evt.tenantId);
    }
  }

  async triggerCompensation(orderId, tenantId) {
    const tenant = this.config.get(tenantId);
    if (tenant.refundRetries >= tenant.maxRefundRetries) {
      await this.outbox.append({
        type: 'CompensatingTransaction',
        orderId,
        tenantId,
        action: 'VOID_PAYMENT'
      });
    }
  }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests understanding of a beginner-friendly, real-world saga with event-sourcing and CQRS: how to coordinate cross-service work, model event contracts, and ensure idempotent handlers with an outbox.

## Key Concepts
- Saga orchestration vs choreography in a write-side workflow
- Event contracts and read-model sketching for status tracking
- Outbox pattern and correlation-based deduplication

## Code Example
```javascript
// Map write events to commands (simplified)
function mapEventToCommand(evt){
  switch(evt.type){
    case 'ContentSubmitted':
      return { type: 'ModerationRequest', payload: { contentId: evt.contentId, correlationId: evt.id } }
    case 'ModerationApproved':
      return { type: 'PublishContent', payload: { contentId: evt.contentId } }
    case 'ModerationRejected':
      return { type: 'HideContent', payload: { contentId: evt.contentId } }
  }
}

// Deduplication (idempotent handler)
if (outbox.has(correlationId)) return; outbox.add(correlationId);
```

